@startuml
title sd - UC1 Obtain sequence statistics
actor Learner
participant "main / standard streams" as Entry
participant "cli.cpp / run" as CLI
participant "cli.cpp / parse_values" as Parser
participant "statistics.cpp / compute_statistics" as Core
Learner -> Entry : numeric tokens, then EOF
Entry -> CLI : run(input, output, error)
CLI -> Parser : parse_values(input)
alt malformed, out-of-range, non-finite token or read failure
  Parser --> CLI : invalid_argument or runtime_error
  CLI -> Entry : error diagnostic to stderr
  CLI --> Entry : return 1
else tokens parsed (possibly empty)
  Parser --> CLI : owning vector<double>
  CLI -> Core : compute_statistics(values)
  note over Core
    Reject empty input first.
    For each value in input order:
    validate finiteness, check addition bounds,
    then update sum and extrema.
  end note
  alt empty, non-finite or overflowing sequence
    Core --> CLI : invalid_argument or overflow_error
    CLI -> Entry : error diagnostic to stderr
    CLI --> Entry : return 1
  else valid sequence
    Core --> CLI : Statistics by value
    CLI -> Entry : write complete formatted summary
    alt output stream failed
      CLI -> Entry : best-effort error diagnostic
      CLI --> Entry : return 1
    else output successful
      CLI --> Entry : return 0
    end
  end
end
Entry --> Learner : output and process exit status
@enduml
